    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run `code/main.py`, then set the round count to 5 and watch diminishing returns. At which round does additional convergence stop?\n2. Add a fourth agent with an adversarial role: always disagree with the current majority. Does this break or improve convergence?\n3. Plot (print) the agreement score per round (fraction of agents on the majority answer). When does it hit 1.0 and is that equivalent to \"correct\"?\n4. Read Du et al. Section 4 ablations. Replicate the \"agents-only\" vs \"rounds-only\" vs \"both\" result using this code.\n5. Read \"Should we be going MAD?\" (arXiv:2311.17371) and list two debate variants beyond round-robin \u2014 e.g., judge-led, chain-of-debate, adversarial."
      ]
    }
